            <ArticleTitle>Young males with primary lymphoma of bone presenting with musculoskeletal pain are prone to be misdiagnosed as ankylosing spondylitis: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>263-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s00296-010-1776-8</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Primary lymphoma of bone (PLB) is an uncommon clinical entity. Pain in the skeleton and pelvis is a frequent complaint which may be partly relieved by nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drugs. So, the patients suffering from PLB are easily referred to the rheumatologist and often be misdiagnosed as rheumatic diseases. Here, we described a case of PLB presenting with rheumatic pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
